nth), each ~20 minutes long\n25: \n26: ### Nemo (@nemo-gta) — The $0 Channel (Same Niche)\n27: - 21.8K subscribers, 116 videos, joined February 2026 (6 months old)\n28: - Total views: 2\n<truncated 4375 bytes>\nhere these creators share knowledge?\n95: - What's the success rate — for every MARINARA making $74K, how many Nemos make $0?\n96: - Are there any YouTube gurus or courses that DO teach this niche? If yes, document them. If no, that itself is a finding.\n97: - Find social media posts (Reddit, Twitter/X, YouTube comments) from people discussing this niche's earning potential\n98: \n99: ## Anti-Sycophancy Enforcement\n100: \n101: Apply these rules throughout the research:\n102: - Challenge every optimistic claim with data. If MARINARA makes $74K, find channels in the same niche making $0 (like Nemo) and calculate the actual success rate.\n103: - Do not present the niche as either \"amazing opportunity\" or \"complete scam.\" Present the data and let the reader decide.\n104: - Every claim must cite a source. No \"some people say\" or \"it's generally believed.\"\n105: - If YouTube gurus have a valid reason to avoid this niche, say so plainly — do not soften it.\n106: - If the niche is genuinely high-risk, quantify the risk (e.g., \"X% of channels in this niche fail to monetize\").\n107: \n108: ## Acceptance Criteria\n109: \n110: ### Research Completeness\n111: - [ ] All 9 angles from R1 are investigated with at least 2 sources each\n112: - [ ] All 8 risk categories from R2 are documented with real examples or data\n113: - [ ] At least one MARINARA video is analyzed (R3)\n114: - [ ] Bull case (R4) is presented with the same rigor as the bear case\n115: - [ ] Every factual claim cites a specific source (URL or data point)\n116: \n117: ### Output Format\n118: - [ ] Single markdown report artifact\n119: - [ ] Sections clearly labeled for each requirement\n120: - [ ] Data tables where applicable (not just prose)\n121: - [ ] TL;DR summary at the top with the 3-5 most 